WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.820 --> 00:00:06.820
55. Man or machine. The strange new world of e-skin.

2
00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:13.820
Chances are you own a computer, smartphone or some other device which gives you information on a screen.

3
00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:16.820
But what if you could be such a device yourself?

4
00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:23.820
With the development of e-skin technology, our path to becoming cyborgs may have just gotten a lot shorter.

5
00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:29.820
Electronic skin, or e-skin, was first created for use on artificial limbs and robots.

6
00:00:30.820 --> 00:00:36.820
Recent improvements, however, have produced a highly flexible plastic film less than two millionths of a meter thick.

7
00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:43.820
This film can be worn directly on human skin and connected to sensors which measure one's heart rate and blood oxygen level.

8
00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:48.820
These measurements are then displayed on the film just as they would be on a computer screen.

9
00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:54.820
And since this new e-skin keeps out water and oxygen, it can be worn for several days.

10
00:00:54.820 --> 00:00:58.820
This allows a person's physical condition to be tracked over time.

11
00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:03.820
But we humans aren't the only ones who could be changed by this strange new technology.

12
00:01:03.820 --> 00:01:09.820
Scientists believe e-skin will soon have the power to give robots an actual sense of touch.

13
00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:16.820
This might enable them to perform surgery and other very delicate tasks without any human involvement at all.

14
00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:22.820
Needless to say, non-medical uses for e-skin are already being planned.

15
00:01:22.820 --> 00:01:28.820
Scientists imagine a time when our feelings and states of mind will be shown right on our bodies.

16
00:01:28.820 --> 00:01:36.820
Tech companies are looking into replacing handheld devices with wearable gadgets whose displays will appear on a person's arm or hand.

17
00:01:36.820 --> 00:01:41.820
The possibilities are amazing, but also more than a little scary.

18
00:01:41.820 --> 00:01:44.820
Right now, we can still believe that people control machines.

19
00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:49.820
But if people are the machines, who will control us?
